    const qcData={shoes:['Confirm both shoes match the ordered model, colour and size','Read the size tag and compare the seller’s sizing system','Check toe shape, heel alignment, sole, stitching and visible glue','Decide whether the box is worth the extra parcel volume','Compare left and right shoes together before approval'],clothing:['Compare chest, length and sleeve measurements where fit matters','Inspect print or embroidery placement, edges and alignment','Check colour, fabric clues, seams, zippers, buttons and lining','Confirm the size tag and selected variant','Estimate fabric weight and bulk before building the parcel'],bags:['Check shape, dimensions, strap length and included accessories','Inspect zippers, pulls, buckles and other hardware','Review stitching, edge paint, lining and logo placement','Decide whether protective packing is needed','Allow for structure and volume in the parcel plan'],electronics:['Confirm exact model, colour, plug and listed accessories','Look for external damage and visible identifiers','Do not assume photos prove battery health or full function','Identify batteries, magnets or route-sensitive attributes','Confirm route eligibility before relying on the item']};
    const articleContent={qc:{title:'How to read five QC photos without missing the expensive detail',html:`<p class="eyebrow">QC field guide · Reviewed August 2026</p><h2>Turn five photos into one clear decision.</h2><p class="lead">Standard warehouse photos are useful when you stop treating them as a gallery. Their job is to answer a small set of purchase questions before an item becomes an international parcel.</p><h3>Begin with the ordered variant</h3><p>Start with what can be checked objectively: model, colour, quantity, size tag and included parts. A visually attractive item can still be wrong. Keep the seller listing and selected option beside the warehouse images, then verify the variant one fact at a time.</p><h3>Use category-specific failure points</h3><table><tr><th>Category</th><th>High-value checks</th><th>Common blind spot</th></tr><tr><td>Shoes</td><td>Both shoes, tags, heel, sole, box choice</td><td>Ignoring parcel volume</td></tr><tr><td>Clothing</td><td>Measurements, print, seams, hardware</td><td>Trusting label size alone</td></tr><tr><td>Bags</td><td>Shape, straps, zippers, accessories</td><td>Missing pieces and volume</td></tr><tr><td>Electronics</td><td>Model, plug, exterior, battery attribute</td><td>Treating QC as a function test</td></tr></table><h3>Request extra evidence only when it changes the decision</h3><p>A useful request names the exact detail and angle: photograph the inside size label straight on, measure the insole from heel to toe, or show the zipper pull and missing strap together. Random extra images add cost without reducing uncertainty.</p><h3>Choose one of four outcomes</h3><p>Approve when visible facts match and limitations are acceptable. Request a retake when an image cannot answer a real question. Exchange when the seller sent the wrong variant but offers a replacement. Return when the mismatch or uncertainty makes international freight a poor bet.</p><h3>Know what photos cannot prove</h3><p>Warehouse images do not automatically prove authenticity, fabric composition, waterproofing, battery health, internal construction or long-term durability. They reduce visible risk; keep the conclusion proportional to the evidence.</p>`},shipping:{title:'Why a light haul can still ship heavy',html:`<p class="eyebrow">Parcel planning · Reviewed August 2026</p><h2>Weight is only half the parcel.</h2><p class="lead">A scale measures mass. A carrier also sells cargo space. That is why light but bulky items can be billed above their actual weight.</p><h3>Understand the comparison</h3><p>A common planning model calculates volumetric weight as length × width × height in centimetres, divided by a route-specific divisor. The chargeable value may be the greater of actual and volumetric weight, often with its own rounding increment.</p><h3>Find the items that create empty space</h3><p>Shoe boxes, puffer jackets, structured bags, rigid gift boxes and protective packing can increase dimensions faster than weight. Identify which item controls the outer box. Removing one low-value retail box can matter more than removing several small accessories.</p><h3>Do not optimise blindly</h3><p>Removing packaging can reduce volume but also reduce protection. A structured bag may crease; glasses may scratch; a shoe box may matter to the buyer. Balance delivered condition, presentation and freight.</p><h3>Compare routes after defining the parcel</h3><p>Destination, sensitive attributes, dimensions, weight and priorities determine which routes are relevant. A cheap ordinary-clothing route may not accept perfume, batteries or another restricted attribute. Check the final route list inside Sugargoo.</p><h3>The planning sequence</h3><ol><li>Estimate bulk before purchase.</li><li>Review QC and decide what packaging stays.</li><li>Calculate actual and volumetric scenarios.</li><li>Confirm attributes and restrictions.</li><li>Compare live routes and final cost in Sugargoo.</li></ol>`},links:{title:'From spreadsheet row to a clean order URL',html:`<p class="eyebrow">Link checks · Reviewed August 2026</p><h2>A product lead is not yet an order.</h2><p class="lead">Spreadsheet rows are fast discovery tools, but sellers change pages, stock, titles and variants. Separate the link you discovered from the listing you are ready to submit.</p><h3>Identify the link type</h3><p>A product detail URL should open one specific item. A shop homepage, search result, image album, shortened mobile share or social post does a different job. If the destination does not expose a clear product, seller and option set, it is not a complete order instruction.</p><h3>Open the live seller page</h3><p>Check that it still represents the same item and offers the expected size, colour, model or batch. Compare price context and domestic freight. A stale spreadsheet title can remain visible after the underlying listing changes.</p><h3>Copy the final URL and write precise remarks</h3><p>Use the complete product-detail URL. Add only information needed to distinguish the order: exact option text, size, colour, quantity and a specific seller instruction. Vague remarks cannot repair an unclear listing.</p><h3>When parsing fails</h3><p>A parser can fail because of a mobile link, login wall, redirect or changed marketplace page. Try the clean final URL. Use a manual order path only when product identity, price, seller and options are clear.</p><h3>Continue checking after purchase</h3><p>The link check prevents one class of error. Warehouse QC is the next checkpoint. Compare the stored item against the selected variant before parcel submission.</p>`},all:{title:'Buyer guide library',html:`<p class="eyebrow">Content architecture</p><h2>Six clusters built to grow.</h2><p class="lead">The deployed site can turn these topics into independent, internally linked pages instead of forcing every query onto one homepage.</p><div class="all-guides-grid"><div class="all-guides-item"><small>Spreadsheet</small><h3>Search, filters and link freshness</h3><p>Product discovery, category pages, dead links and clean URLs.</p></div><div class="all-guides-item"><small>QC photos</small><h3>Warehouse decisions</h3><p>Checklists, retakes, measurements, returns and exchanges.</p></div><div class="all-guides-item"><small>Shipping</small><h3>Weight, volume and routes</h3><p>Packaging, rehearsal, tracking and insurance.</p></div><div class="all-guides-item"><small>Marketplaces</small><h3>Taobao, Weidian and 1688</h3><p>Seller pages, variants, MOQ and parser issues.</p></div><div class="all-guides-item"><small>Payments</small><h3>Costs and account actions</h3><p>Item cost, balance, refunds, coupons and support.</p></div><div class="all-guides-item"><small>Buyer evidence</small><h3>Arrival and haul research</h3><p>Public examples used as context, never a guarantee.</p></div></div>`}};
    const checklist=document.getElementById('checklist');function renderChecklist(k){checklist.innerHTML=qcData[k].map(x=>`<li>${x}</li>`).join('')}renderChecklist('shoes');document.querySelectorAll('[data-qc]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-qc]').forEach(x=>x.classList.remove('active'));b.classList.add('active');renderChecklist(b.dataset.qc)});
    function calculate(){const actualInput=document.getElementById('weight'),lengthInput=document.getElementById('length'),widthInput=document.getElementById('width'),heightInput=document.getElementById('height'),divisorInput=document.getElementById('divisor'),chargeOutput=document.getElementById('chargeable'),typeOutput=document.getElementById('weightType');let a=+actualInput.value||0,v=((+lengthInput.value||0)*(+widthInput.value||0)*(+heightInput.value||0))/(+divisorInput.value||6000),c=Math.max(a,v);chargeOutput.textContent=c.toFixed(2)+' kg';typeOutput.textContent=v>a?'Volumetric weight controls':'Actual weight controls'}['weight','length','width','height','divisor'].forEach(x=>document.getElementById(x).oninput=calculate);calculate();
    document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{let i=b.closest('.faq-item'),o=i.classList.toggle('open');b.setAttribute('aria-expanded',o)});
    const drawer=document.getElementById('drawer'),menuBtn=document.getElementById('menuBtn');function closeDrawer(){drawer.classList.remove('open');document.body.classList.remove('lock');menuBtn.textContent='☰';menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false')}menuBtn.onclick=()=>{let o=!drawer.classList.contains('open');drawer.classList.toggle('open',o);document.body.classList.toggle('lock',o);menuBtn.textContent=o?'×':'☰';menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded',o)};drawer.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(a=>a.onclick=closeDrawer);
    const toast=document.getElementById('toast'),catalogSearch=document.getElementById('catalogSearch'),searchInput=document.getElementById('searchInput');let tt;function toastMsg(m){toast.textContent=m;toast.classList.add('show');clearTimeout(tt);tt=setTimeout(()=>toast.classList.remove('show'),2500)}catalogSearch.onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();let q=searchInput.value.trim();if(!q)return toastMsg('Enter a product, brand or style first.');window.open('https://kakobuymake.com/?m=home&c=Search&a=lists&keywords='+encodeURIComponent(q),'_blank','noopener')};
    const modal=document.getElementById('modal'),modalTitle=document.getElementById('modalTitle'),articleBody=document.getElementById('articleBody'),allGuides=document.getElementById('allGuides');function openArticle(k){modalTitle.textContent=articleContent[k].title;articleBody.innerHTML=articleContent[k].html;modal.classList.add('open');document.body.classList.add('lock');modal.querySelector('.modal-panel').scrollTop=0}function closeArticle(){modal.classList.remove('open');document.body.classList.remove('lock')}document.querySelector('.modal-close').onclick=closeArticle;modal.onclick=e=>{if(e.target===modal)closeArticle()};document.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.key==='Escape'){closeArticle();closeDrawer()}};
